  "query_preview": "..Today...An upper low is currently centered over \neastern NV and moving to the northeast. This feature brought a \nminor surge in moisture and instability this morning, with weak \nisolated showers and thunderstorms across NW AZ. Showers in this \nregion have ended as the trough lifts northeastward, and a weak \ncut-off low will be left behind off the coast of Baja California. \nMeanwhile, a shortwave currently located over Mexico will be \nslowly drifting northward over the next few days, following a \ntrajectory into NM and eastern AZ. A much larger surge of moisture\nwill accompany this feature. PW values this afternoon will reach \nabove the 95th percentile for this time of year across eastern AZ.\nScattered showers and thunderstorms are firing mainly near the \nAZ-NM border as of 1200 MST. This activity is forecast to \nincrease in coverage and continue through the afternoon and \novernight. A few instances of flash flooding will be possible \nacross Navajo and Apache counties today. \n\nWednesday and Thursday...By tomorrow, the main axis of the wave \nripples through our area. Moisture will spread further west, and \nshower/thunderstorm chances will extend to Coconino and Yavapai \ncounties. Further east, rainfall may transition into more of a \nstratiform type, however heavy accumulations are still possible. \nThe WPC excessive rainfall outlook puts most of northern AZ in a \nmarginal risk for flash flooding tomorrow. On Thursday, the \naforementioned low off the coast of Baja California makes a push \ninland. The result will be continued showers and thunderstorms \nacross much of northern AZ. \n\nFriday and onward...Ensemble guidance tends to bring a downturn in \nactivity on Friday then more so on Saturday after the wave \ndeparts and brief ridging with drier air remain dominant. By early\nnext week there is considerable uncertainty hinging on a pair of \ntropical systems and a Pacific trough that may form. The current \nforecast calls for a widespread area of 30-60% PoPs across \nnorthern AZ on Monday, however there is a lot of room for this to \nchange.",
